A bind moves a thread its caller holds only a narrowed capability to.
A process given a thread to look at could stop it, or move it off the units its owner gave it;
a call binds only a thread its caller could control.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call bound a thread its caller could not control to units

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -732,7 +732,7 @@ static int op_time(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
             return KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         }
         struct cap tc;
-        int err = slot_lookup_typed(t, arg[1], CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, &tc);
+        int err = slot_lookup_typed(t, arg[1], CAP_THREAD, 0, &tc);
         if (err != KERR_OK) {
             return err;
         }
